# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid node266
node266 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>ibid</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Business Identifier (IBID) &lt;https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/&gt; is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the ISO/DIS 25500-3 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html&gt; draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (|) (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420).&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Business Identifier (IBID) &lt;https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/&gt; is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the ISO/DIS 25500-3 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html&gt; draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (|) (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420).&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/SpdxDocument node267
node267 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>SpdxDocument</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/SpdxDocument' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/SpdxDocument</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;A collection of SPDX Elements that could potentially be serialized.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;A collection of SPDX Elements that could potentially be serialized.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;The SpdxDocument provides a convenient way to express information about
collections of SPDX Elements that could potentially be serialized as complete
units (e.g., all in-scope SPDX data within a single JSON-LD file).

SpdxDocument is independent of any particular serialization format or instance.

Information we wish to preserve about a specific instance of serialization of
this SPDX content is NOT expressed using the SpdxDocument but rather using an
associated Artifact representing a particular instance of SPDX data physical
serialization.

Any instance of serialization of SPDX data shall not contain more than one
SpdxDocument element definition.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
