# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/standardCompliance node461
node461 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>standardCompliance</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/standardCompliance' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/standardCompliance</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;A standard with which the artifact complies.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;A standard with which the artifact complies.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;A free-form textual description that captures a standard with which the
artifact complies.

The standard may, but is not necessarily required to, satisfy a legal or
regulatory requirement.

If the artifact is using a standard as a reference or guideline, but not
necessarily compliant with it, use the /Core/standardName property instead.

For a detailed compliance information, please consider defining
a /Core/Relationship with &quot;conformsTo&quot; relationship type to
a /Core/Regulation.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
